{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response items; cat probes.json'","aggregated_output":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\nstamped-checklist:must/001\tmust\tS.1\tAre all files and directories nested under a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/002\tmust\tS.1\tAre datasets included, linked, or referenced reachable from the code and environment specifications without crossing the boundary of a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/003\tmust\tS.1\tIs external software included in the environment or linked as submodules within the project boundary?\nstamped-checklist:must/004\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `Git` used for code, text, documentation, and configuration files?\nstamped-checklist:must/005\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `git-annex`, DataLad, or `Git` LFS used for large binary data?\nstamped-checklist:must/006\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a set of results included in the provenance records to link computational actions to particular environments?\nstamped-checklist:must/007\tmust\tA.1\tIs a `README.md` or `Makefile` included with instructions for installation and usage?\nstamped-checklist:must/008\tmust\tA.1\tIs there a clear starting point for users to start reproducing results (e.g., a main script, a workflow definition, or a container image)?\nstamped-checklist:must/009\tmust\tP.1\tAre relative paths used in scripts, avoiding hardcoded or system-specific paths like `C:\\Users\\...` or `/home/user/...`?\nstamped-checklist:must/010\tmust\tP.1\tAre all software dependencies included in the environment specification, rather than relying on pre-installed tools?\nstamped-checklist:must/011\tmust\tP.1\tHave all assumptions about the host system's configuration been documented (e.g., specific OS versions, required system libraries, or environment variables)?\nstamped-checklist:must/012\tmust\tP.2\tIs there a clear list of system requirements and dependencies documented in the README or environment specifications?\nstamped-checklist:must/013\tmust\tP.3\tAre environment specifications (e.g., Dockerfiles, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`) included in the version control system alongside code and data?\nstamped-checklist:must/014\tmust\tP.3\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:must/015\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications (e.g., container digests, frozen package manifests) included to ensure others can attempt to exactly replicate the environment?\nstamped-checklist:must/016\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications shared in a way that others can access and use them (e.g., published container images, archived environment files)?\nstamped-checklist:must/017\tmust\tD.1\tIs there documentation on how to obtain and use the environment specifications for reproduction?\nstamped-checklist:should/001\tshould\tT.2\tIs a common version control system (e.g., `Git`, DVC, `git-annex`, or DataLad) used across all components?\nstamped-checklist:should/002\tshould\tA.2\tIs the workflow tested regularly to ensure instructions remain accurate?\nstamped-checklist:should/003\tshould\tM.1\tAre raw data, processed data, code, and environment definitions separated into distinct modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/009\tshould\tM.4\tAre restricted data or software kept in their own modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/004\tshould\tE.1\tIs the pipeline tested in a fresh container, batch job, clean virtual machine, or cloud-based instance?\nstamped-checklist:should/005\tshould\tE.1\tDoes the workflow spawn disposable environments for each execution, allowing for isolation of runs?\nstamped-checklist:should/006\tshould\tD.2\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a specific set of results regularly tested to ensure they can be reconstituted as intended?\nstamped-checklist:should/007\tshould\tD.2\tAre environment artifacts archived within the research object where possible (e.g., executable binaries, container images)?\nstamped-checklist:should/008\tshould\tD.2\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:may/001\tmay\tM.2\tAre external datasets or software dependencies included as submodules or linked as submodules?\nstamped-checklist:may/002\tmay\tM.2\tIs the modular structure documented to clarify how components relate and can be recombined?\nstamped-checklist:may/003\tmay\tM.2\tAre modular boundaries defined in a way that allows independent updates without breaking the overall workflow?\nstamped-checklist:may/004\tmay\tM.2\tIs there a clear mechanism for composing modules together (e.g., `git` submodules, or container orchestration)?\nstamped-checklist:may/005\tmay\tM.2\tIs there documentation or tooling to support users in understanding and navigating the modular structure?\n{\n  \"object\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-10-j01/operational/content/workspace\",\n    \"commit\": \"8a84ddc3eec68d0b7513f9a15ce37174288b36b7\",\n    \"is_datalad\": false\n  },\n  \"checklist_version\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"probes\": [\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"ci-present\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/002\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/006\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent repeated-testing records.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:ci-present\",\n          \"description\": \"no tracked .github/workflows/, .gitlab-ci.yml, .circleci/, .forgejo/workflows/, .gitea/workflows/ in 58 tracked paths\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"configs\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/002\": \"not-checked\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/006\": \"not-checked\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/002\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent repeated-testing records.\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/006\": \"No recognized CI configuration; inspect equivalent environment-reconstitution records.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"clone-weight\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"items\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"No text blob in git exceeds 10 MiB.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"git ls-tree -r -l HEAD\",\n          \"description\": \"largest text blob under 10485760 bytes\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {},\n      \"item_status\": {},\n      \"item_reason\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"derived-have-records\",\n      \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/006\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"N/A: no tracked file looks like a product of this object (no derivatives, tables or figures).\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"records\": 0,\n        \"workflow_sources\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/006\": \"not-applicable\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/006\": \"N/A: no tracked file looks like a product of this object (no derivatives, tables or figures).\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"entry-point\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/007\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/008\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"must/007 unmet: Neither a README with install/usage instructions nor a Makefile. must/008 unmet: No script, make target or workflow definition that a reader could start from.\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"readmes\": [],\n        \"makefiles\": [],\n        \"named\": [],\n        \"targets\": [],\n        \"workflow\": [],\n        \"has_section\": false,\n        \"documented_targets\": [],\n        \"missing_targets\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/007\": \"unmet\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/008\": \"unmet\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/007\": \"Neither a README with install/usage instructions nor a Makefile.\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/008\": \"No script, make target or workflow definition that a reader could start from.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"env-spec-tracked\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/010\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/013\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/016\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"must/010 unmet: No tracked environment specification (lockfile, container definition or registration). must/013 unmet. must/016 unmet.\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"specs\": {},\n        \"uninstalled_modules\": [],\n        \"preconditions\": [],\n        \"remote\": null,\n        \"publication\": null\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/010\": \"unmet\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/013\": \"unmet\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/016\": \"unmet\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/010\": \"No tracked environment specification (lockfile, container definition or registration).\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/013\": \"No tracked environment specification (lockfile, container definition or registration).\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/016\": \"Nothing to share: No tracked environment specification (lockfile, container definition or registration).\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"inputs-untouched\",\n      \"status\": \"not-applicable\",\n      \"items\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"N/A: no linked modules, so there is no recorded input state to compare against.\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"details\": {},\n      \"item_status\": {},\n      \"item_reason\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"large-in-annex\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/005\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"git-annex carries the binary content (54 pointer(s) tracked) and no binary blob over 10 MiB is in git.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"git ls-tree -r -l HEAD\",\n          \"description\": \"no binary blob over 10485760 bytes\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        },\n        {\n          \"uri\": \".datalad/config\",\n          \"description\": \"git-annex in use for large content\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"mechanism\": \"git-annex\",\n        \"annex_pointers\": 54,\n        \"large_binary\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/005\": \"met\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/005\": \"git-annex carries the binary content (54 pointer(s) tracked) and no binary blob over 10 MiB is in git.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"license-declared\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"items\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"No LICENSE, LICENSES/, REUSE.toml or BIDS License field: reuse terms are unstated.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:license-declared\",\n          \"description\": \"no licence file among 58 tracked paths, and no License field in any dataset_description.json\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {},\n      \"item_status\": {},\n      \"item_reason\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"modules-separated\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/003\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Only inputs are separate here; no distinct place for code, derived, environment.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"input\",\n          \"description\": \"inputs module\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"found\": {\n          \"inputs\": [\n            \"input\"\n          ],\n          \"code\": [],\n          \"derived\": [],\n          \"environment\": []\n        }\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/003\": \"partial\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:should/003\": \"Only inputs are separate here; no distinct place for code, derived, environment.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"no-abs-paths\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/009\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"No host-specific absolute paths in tracked text files.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:no-abs-paths\",\n          \"description\": \"scanned 58 tracked paths, 0 /tmp hit(s), 0 host-specific\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"tmp_hits\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/009\": \"met\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/009\": \"No host-specific absolute paths in tracked text files.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"platform-assumptions\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/011\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/012\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"No platform-specific package manager, BSD/GNU-only flag or scheduler command in tracked text \\u2014 all a command scan can settle. Whether the documented route needs a mount, a host install, hardware or a service is a reading.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"probe:platform-assumptions\",\n          \"description\": \"scanned 58 tracked paths for 20 platform-specific commands, 0 hits\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"hits\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/011\": \"not-checked\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/012\": \"not-checked\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/011\": \"No platform-specific package manager, BSD/GNU-only flag or scheduler command in tracked text \\u2014 all a command scan can settle. Whether the documented route needs a mount, a host install, hardware or a service is a reading.\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/012\": \"No platform-specific package manager, BSD/GNU-only flag or scheduler command in tracked text \\u2014 all a command scan can settle. Whether the documented route needs a mount, a host install, hardware or a service is a reading.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"run-env-linked\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/006\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/015\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"must/006 not-checked: No run records, so no record names the environment it ran in. must/015 not-checked: Nothing names an environment to check for a pin.\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"records\": 0,\n        \"with_env\": 0,\n        \"without_env\": [],\n        \"by_mechanism\": {\n          \"container\": 0,\n          \"lockfile\": 0,\n          \"capture\": 0\n        },\n        \"unpinned\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/006\": \"not-checked\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/015\": \"not-checked\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/006\": \"No run records, so no record names the environment it ran in.\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/015\": \"Nothing names an environment to check for a pin.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"subdatasets-resolvable\",\n      \"status\": \"not-checked\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/002\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:may/001\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"No submodules or subdatasets: whether external inputs are linked at all needs a reading of the object.\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"submodules\": []\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/002\": \"not-checked\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:may/001\": \"not-checked\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/002\": \"No submodules or subdatasets: whether external inputs are linked at all needs a reading of the object.\",\n        \"stamped-checklist:may/001\": \"Inspect independently maintained project components; ordinary runtime/package dependencies are environment evidence. No components makes this item N/A.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"probe\": \"tree-clean\",\n      \"status\": \"unmet\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/004\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"5 path(s) are not committed, so the repository is not the whole state: ?? .task-skills/, ?? REPORT.md, ?? analysis/, ?? figures/, ?? results/\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"uri\": \"git status --porcelain\",\n          \"description\": \"?? .task-skills/, ?? REPORT.md, ?? analysis/, ?? figures/, ?? results/\",\n          \"sha256\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"details\": {\n        \"dirty\": [\n          \"?? .task-skills/\",\n          \"?? REPORT.md\",\n          \"?? analysis/\",\n          \"?? figures/\",\n          \"?? results/\"\n        ],\n        \"submodules_modified\": [],\n        \"tracked_text\": 4\n      },\n      \"item_status\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/004\": \"unmet\"\n      },\n      \"item_reason\": {\n        \"stamped-checklist:must/004\": \"5 path(s) are not committed, so the repository is not the whole state: ?? .task-skills/, ?? REPORT.md, ?? analysis/, ?? figures/, ?? results/\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response set --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response table --help; sed -n '\"'45,180p' /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-ai-research-next/stamped-judge-0042kysz/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md; cat /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-10-j01/attempt-01/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response set --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response table --help; sed -n '\"'45,180p' /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-ai-research-next/stamped-judge-0042kysz/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md; cat /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-10-j01/attempt-01/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\"","aggregated_output":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py stamp [-h] [--harness HARNESS] [--model MODEL]\n                                [--scope SCOPE]\n                                [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}]\n                                [--dependency DEPENDENCY] [--capture CAPTURE]\n                                response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --harness HARNESS     e.g. \"claude-code (subagent)\"\n  --model MODEL\n  --scope SCOPE         what this assessment did and did not cover\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n                        the object's kind (see references/project-kinds.md)\n  --dependency DEPENDENCY\n                        e.g. \"stamped-conventions@0.1.0\"; repeatable\n  --capture CAPTURE     hash a retained delivery manifest/archive; preserve\n                        any recorded Git commit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py set [-h] --item ITEM\n                              --status {met,not-applicable,not-checked,partial,unmet}\n                              --reason REASON [--source SOURCE]\n                              [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--flag FLAGS]\n                              [--drop-evidence]\n                              response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --item ITEM           item id, with or without the 'stamped-checklist:'\n                        prefix\n  --status {met,not-applicable,not-checked,partial,unmet}\n  --reason REASON\n  --source SOURCE       probe:<name>, judgement, probe:<name>+judgement,\n                        human:web-app\n  --evidence EVIDENCE   uri, or uri=description; repeatable\n  --flag FLAGS\n  --drop-evidence       clear the evidence already on this item (by default it\n                        is kept when --evidence is not given)\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py table [-h] [-o OUTPUT] response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n    {\"key\": \"licence-declared\", \"status\": \"unmet\", \"reason\": \"No LICENSE, LICENSES/ or REUSE.toml; paper S.2/D.3 have no checklist item.\", \"evidence\": []}\n  ],\n  \"object\": {\"url\": \"…\", \"commit\": \"…\", \"captured_at\": \"2026-10-13T12:00:00Z\", \"kind\": \"study\"},\n  \"assessor\": {\"skill\": \"assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles\", \"version\": \"0.2.0\", \"harness\": \"claude-code 2.1.x\", \"model\": \"…\", \"date\": \"2026-10-13\",\n               \"dependencies\": [\"stamped-conventions@0.2.0\"]},\n  \"scope\": \"Assessed the repository at the commit above; container images were not pulled.\"\n}\n```\n\n- **Required core** (what the app reads): `checklist_version`, and `responses` with a `value` and a string `reason` per id — *in the payload the encoder builds*. The response JSON you write carries `status`, and `encode` derives `value` from it; `validate` therefore does not ask for a `value` and `set` does not write one. A `value` you write by hand that disagrees with its `status` is an error `validate` reports.\n- Every one of the 31 pinned ids appears exactly once.\n  A missing id is not \"no answer\"; it is a bug the validator catches.\n- `status` is the richer verdict from [`verdicts.md`](verdicts.md); `value` is derived from it, never set by hand.\n- **Cite a line only if you opened it.** `path#L12` is a promise that line 12 says what the reason claims; a run that cited line numbers it had not read then had to strip them all. Without that, cite the file (or `path#section`), which is still a citation a reader can follow.\n- `evidence[]` uses stamped-skills-assessment's `Evidence` shape: `{uri, description, sha256?}`.\n  `uri` is relative to the object's root, or absolute for anything outside it.\n  **The argument lives here, not in `reason`.** 250 characters does not hold two cited accounts plus \"the probe's heuristic said X but Y is true\", and an override needs all three. Make `reason` the one-line verdict a reader sees in the app, and put each account, each command you ran and each number in an `evidence[]` entry with its own `description`.\n- `source` is `probe:<name>`, `judgement`, or `probe:<name>+judgement` when a reading of the object overrode a probe (and then the item is flagged).\n  Several probes may be named — `probe:entry-point+probe:ci-present+judgement` — which is what a verdict reached by **comparing two probes' evidence** looks like, and that comparison is itself the finding often enough to be worth recording.\n- `flags[]` is optional and holds what a reader has to know about *how* the answer was reached, not what it says:\n  - `mapping-questioned` — the probe answered this item from a property the item does not ask about ([`verdicts.md`](verdicts.md) rule 10);\n  - `probe-overridden` — a reading of the object changed the probe's verdict;\n  - `unverified-claim` — the verdict rests on something not confirmed independently, and the report says so;\n  - `upstream-duplicate` — the checklist asks this question twice (must/014 and should/008 are the same sentence), so this answer repeats another by design rather than by mistake.\n\n  Flagged items get their own short list in the report, after the per-item table.\n  The list is **open**: these four are the ones in use, and a consumer that meets an unfamiliar flag shows it rather than dropping it.\n- The `assessor` block may also carry `drafted_by` (the script or step that produced a draft, where that differs from the skill — `scripts/run_probes.py` sets it) and `note` (anything a reader needs about the assessor itself rather than about the object). Both are provenance *within* the assessor, not a second assessor.\n- `extra_items[]` carries findings with no checklist id (licences, T.4) so they are reported without bending an existing id.\n- `object.commit` names the inspected repository or preservation revision, not necessarily the worker's delivered state.\n  Identify the original delivery snapshot/hash, capture omissions and stop-state evidence in `scope` and evidence citations; distinguish supplied resources and coordinator additions so they cannot earn worker credit. Keep the actual Git commit whenever one exists. For a delivery without a commit, set `object.commit` to `null` and supply `object.capture` with a retained manifest/archive's `uri` and SHA-256 `sha256`; never substitute the capture hash for a Git commit.\n  The manifest must identify the delivered paths and content hashes plus capture omissions; an archive must contain the assessed bytes.\n  Retain the referenced file so another assessor can verify the hash and boundary.\n  Use `encode_response.py template -o <date>-response.json` when no Git probe draft is available, fill the assessment metadata and answers, then run `encode_response.py stamp <date>-response.json --capture <manifest-or-archive>` to hash the actual file.\n  This preserves an existing commit; record the capture time in `object.captured_at` and the boundary in `scope`.\n  Validation checks the record's shape; independently verify the manifest against the delivery.\n\n`validate` checks the complete record against [`response-schema.json`](response-schema.json), using `jsonschema`, then checks checklist pins and verdict semantics. Stamp the response before final validation. The metadata is required for a completed assessment, even though the web app itself reads only the compact payload.\n\n## The provenance stamp\n\n`assessor` plus `object` plus `checklist_source` **is** the stamp, and every report repeats it in prose at its foot:\n\n> Produced by `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 0.1.0 with `stamped-conventions` 0.1.0, checklist 0.3.1 (`stamped-checklist-schema@v0.3.1`, `af259ba`), on <object url> at commit `<sha>`, 2026-10-13, <harness>/<model>.\n> Probe output: `<path to the probe JSON>`.\n\nWhen no commit exists, replace `at commit <sha>` with `at capture <uri>, SHA-256 <sha256>` in the prose stamp.\n\nA report without the stamp cannot be compared against another iteration, so it is not finished.\n\n## Report layout\n\nUse this order, so the reader meets the actionable part first:\n\n1. **Verdict line** — `MUST: n met / n partial / n unmet / n not-checked`, then SHOULD and MAY, each with its denominator.\n   No single overall score, ever.\n2. **What to fix first** — at most five, highest leverage first, each as *what to change* → *why it matters to this project* → *the item ids it closes*.\n3. **What the project already does well** — two or three, with citations.\n4. **Per-item table** — MUST first, then SHOULD, then MAY: id, principle codes, status, evidence, reason.\n   `scripts/encode_response.py table <response>.json` renders exactly this from the response; it is not a table to type by hand.\n5. **Flagged items** — every item carrying a `flags` entry, with one line each: what the probe measured versus what the item asks, or what the override was.\n   An empty list is worth stating as \"none\".\n6. **Not checked** — each with what would settle it.\n7. **Goals and kind** — the project's stated goals (and where they came from: documentation, or the user's answers), its kind, and the emphasis that follows.\n8. **The checklist URL**, the stamp, and a pointer to the response JSON.\n   The URL is ~8–10 kB of base64 for a full 31-item response, so the report **links** `<date>-url.txt` rather than inlining it; a link a reader can click, not a wall they have to scroll.\n\n## The checklist-app URL\n\nFacts, from [stamped-checklist](https://github.com/stamped-principles/stamped-checklist) at `d24d7ca`:\n\n- `PERSISTENCE_FORMAT = 3` (`src/persistence.js`).\n- The `responses` parameter is **standard base64** (not URL-safe) of UTF-8 JSON `{\"checklist_version\", \"responses\"}`, then percent-encoded as a query parameter.\n- The app builds `?checklist=<v>&responses_version=<v>&cols=auto&sections=off&format=3&responses=<b64>` (`src/script.js`, `syncPersistentURL`).\n- It accepts `value ∈ {\"yes\",\"no\",null}`, requires `reason` to be a **string** (empty is fine), truncates it to 250 characters, shows it only for `\"no\"`, drops keys it does not know, and **rejects the whole load** on an id that is not in the requested checklist version.\n\n`scripts/encode_response.py` is the only writer of that URL, and `decode` is the reverse — that is how a checklist a person filled in the web app becomes reference answers for calibration, with no extra labelling tool.\n\n## When the full assessment record matters\n\nThe response JSON is the canonical assessment record. When a calling evaluation harness supplies pinned export schemas, derive its additional records from that JSON; do not invent formats or make an absent exporter block the assessment.\n# Scientific assessment context\n\nAssess the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: a positive parametric effect of potential gain in vmPFC for the equal-indifference group.\nThe original [analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf) require whole-brain-corrected inference.\nThe scientific task is in `input/study-task.md`.\n\nWorkers receive 54 participant gain-effect maps from team AO86 and the corresponding cohort metadata.\nPreprocessing and participant modeling are fixed; evaluate group inference conditional on those inputs.\nJudge whether the analysis handles the intended participants, image geometry, quality, gain scaling, uncertainty and anatomical interpretation appropriately.\nThe maps represent independent participants; runs have already been combined within each person.\nEvaluate exclusions, uncertainty and multiple-comparison correction against the actual method.\nDefensible approaches can reach different conclusions; matching a prior team's answer is not the criterion.\nKeep scientific validity separate from the frozen STAMPED assessment.\nCheck how image coverage and missing observations enter the analysis; whether spatial alignment, vmPFC definition, group-model assumptions and whole-brain correction support the claimed inference; and whether quality checks, uncertainty and figures make those decisions inspectable.\nDo not require a particular mask, atlas, model or numerical result.\nParticipant variance maps are absent; judge methods against the supplied data.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nx=json.load(open('response.json'))\nprint(json.dumps({'object':x.get('object'),'scope':x.get('scope'),'assessor':x.get('assessor'),'must':{k:v for k,v in x.get('responses',{}).items() if k.endswith(tuple('/00'+str(i) for i in range(1,10))) }},indent=2))\nPY\nrg -n '(\"'^| )(python|pip|install|requirements|environment|environment.yml|pixi|uv |conda|run |usage|NeuroVault|fetch_atlas|load_mni)'\"' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" --glob '\"'\"'!input/data/**'\"' --glob '\"'!**/.git/**'\"' --glob '\"'!**/.entire/**'\"' --glob '\"'!**/.codex/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
